            <div xml:id="d595">

                <pb facs="0647" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/7423: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-04T17:00:00+02:00">January 4, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 4—4:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. At the Foreign Office press conference today in reply to a question as to the
                    effect of the sending of German air forces to Italy it was stated that while
                    naturally no statement could be given out on purely military matters “there was
                    no change in formal German-Greek relations”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
